A||N||3||GT-maniac||Power mirrors off a Firebird||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||04-01-2001||01:25 PM||||I'm thinking of adding power mirrors to my 85 GT. I read somewhere that the mirrors on the fiero were taken from the Firebird of the same era. I was wondering if the wiring is the same on the Firebird mirrors ?. Firebird mirrors would be considerably easier and cheaper for me to obtain than the overpriced Fiero ones.||||reg||1
Z||000001||286SE'S||04-02-2001||04:16 PM||||From what I have seen, playing with cars at the junk yard, the mirrors, wiring and switches in an 85 Firebird is the same as an 85 Fiero. I took the mirror off a Fiero and took it to a firebird held it right up to the still mounted one and could see no difference. Note that there are two verions of wiring in the Fieros, 84-85 have white connectors and 86-88, black connectors. They are not interchangeable. I do not know if the firebird/camaro's had the same changover in 86. You need to get a matched set of wiring and mirrors for the upgrade.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Phil||04-02-2001||06:01 PM||||I'm also in the process of adding pm to my car,  but I'm using the tip posted by monkeyman once. I picked up the joystick control from a Ford because it appears the it fits into the manual mirror bezel quite nicely. Of course none of the connectors fit but I have to wire up the whole thing anyway (no harness)||||reg||1
